course: dictionary
lesson: 5033
title: Starting and joining: the word initiate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Initiate» is a formal word, used mostly in stories, history and exam writing. To initiate something means to start it. «Initiate a plan» means start a plan, and «initiate contact» means make the first move to talk to someone.
explain: Some groups welcome new members with a special ceremony, a formal event with set words or actions. To initiate someone into a group means to let them join, often through this ceremony. A person who has just been let in is an initiate.
explain: The sentence «Initiated Sikhs, who have made special promises in a ceremony, wear the five Ks» gives you the clues. The ceremony is the formal event, and the promises are what happens in it. So initiated here means having joined through that ceremony.
fact: «Initiate» means to start something, or to let someone join a group.
fact: An «initiate» is a person who has just been allowed to join a group or learn its secrets.
fact: «Initiated Sikhs» have made special promises in a ceremony, and they wear the five Ks, including uncut hair (kesh) and a steel bracelet (kara).
fact: In a computer, to initiate a download means to start it.
fact: A good check is to swap in «start»: «initiate a plan» becomes «start a plan», and it still makes sense.
exercise: «Initiate a plan» means what? | Throw away a plan | Read a plan slowly | Hide a plan | *Start a plan
exercise: «Initiated Sikhs, who have made special promises in a ceremony, wear the five Ks.» Where did the initiated Sikhs make their promises? | Under the sea | At school during a test | *In a ceremony | In a shop
exercise: What is an «initiate»? | A computer that stops downloads | *A person who has just been allowed to join a group | A very old castle | A steel bracelet worn on the wrist
test: Which word means start? | Hide | Ignore | Forgive | *Initiate
test: To initiate someone into a group means what? | *Let them join, often with a special ceremony | Stop them from speaking | Send them home early | Wash their hair
exam: In the sentence «Initiated Sikhs, who have made special promises in a ceremony», what does initiated mean? | Stopped wearing jewellery | *Joined a group through a formal ceremony with special promises | Went to school late | Lost their way
